INT. FLOODED TERRACE BUNKER - NIGHT

Knee-deep water. A single lantern swings from a hook. Mortar fire thumps overhead; dust sifts down.

SGT. TAMSIN BRIGG (40s, mud to the eyebrows) checks a rifle bolt. CPL. IVO PETROV (30s) holds a radio that gives only static. PVT. LUKA "MOTH" DEMIR (19) crouches by the slit, shaking.

BRIGG
Heads down, everybody. Quiet.

Another thump. They flatten against the wall. Water slops. Brigg and Petrov grab for the lantern at the same moment and both stop with their hands on the hook.

PETROV
(to Brigg)
Radio's dead, Sergeant.

BRIGG
Then we're the radio.

MOTH
(mutters, to himself)
Don't look. Don't look. Don't look.

The hatch above scrapes. All three raise their rifles. A boot, then a body drops into the water. MEDIC ABENA NKRUMAH (20s, red cross armband, medic bag held overhead) lands in a crouch.

ABENA
Hold your fire. Who's bleeding?

Nobody answers. Moth slowly lowers his rifle and looks at his own hand, which is slick and dark.

BRIGG
(quietly)
Moth. Show me.
